//==
// # Repair diagnosis over one index: types (complexity sweep, chunk L8)
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Face rows
//  - The repair index

//==
// # Face rows

// Faces grouped by an integer key, in compressed rows: row k is Faces[Offsets[k]] up to
// Faces[Offsets[k + 1]], in the order the faces were given, possibly with repeats. Offsets has
// one entry per row plus one, starts at 0 and ends at Faces.Count; there is a row for every key
// from 0 to the largest key given. The stdlib's JaggedArray holds the same data, but the C#
// writer emits no member for a library function whose first parameter is an instance of a
// generic type, so the row accessors need a concrete receiver.
type FaceRows
    implements IValue
{
    Offsets: Array<Integer>;
    Faces: Array<BrepFaceIndex>;
}

//==
// # The repair index

// What layer 11's diagnosis asks of a model, built once per plan: whether each face is in a closed
// shell (IsClosedShell, once per shell), the uses of every edge in each shell (layer 2's
// EdgeUseTable), the faces of every edge (EdgeFaceTable), and the faces by end vertex, by curve,
// by surface and by loop, and every face. Built only by RepairIndexCounted. Removes: a whole-model
// scan per defect in PlanOf (IsInClosedShell, UseCount, FacesAtVertex, FacesOnCurve,
// FacesOnSurface, FacesOfLoop).
type RepairIndex
{
    ClosedShellFaces: Array<Boolean>;
    ShellUses: Array<EdgeUseTable>;
    EdgeFaces: EdgeFaceTable;
    VertexFaces: FaceRows;
    CurveFaces: FaceRows;
    SurfaceFaces: FaceRows;
    LoopFaces: FaceRows;
    AllFaces: Array<BrepFaceIndex>;
}
